{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Before Baal-zephon.</b> It alone remained of all the gods of Egypt, etc., and we must give a reason why this one survived more than the other deities. It appears from this that they had many idols, for they worshipped many constellations, since every constellation has a particular power and influence over a specific matter. And Baal-zephon is the idol which they thought would influence gold and an abundance of pearls for them, as it is written (Job 37:22), ״מִצָּפוֹן זָהָב יֶאֱתֶה״ ('Out of the north comes gold'). And the Holy One, blessed be He, left specifically this idol in order to deceive them, so that they would say that this idol would avenge their disgrace over the fact that Israel had taken their money unjustly. For in all the other plagues, Pharaoh justified the judgment upon himself, saying that they came upon him justly and justly did their heavenly officers also suffer. But regarding the money, Pharaoh thought that Israel had taken their wealth not with righteousness and not with justice; therefore Baal-zephon remained, so that they would say 'their fear is strong' and it would demand from Israel the money they had borrowed. And this is what it says: ״וַיֵּהָפֵךְ לְבַב פַּרְעֹה״ ('and the heart of Pharaoh was turned'), etc. — Rashi explained: on account of their money that they had borrowed. And what they said, ״כִּי שִׁלַּחְנוּ אֶת יִשְׂרָאֵל מֵעָבְדֵנוּ״ ('for we have sent Israel away from serving us') — because whatever a slave acquires, his master acquires, and the main substance of his words was for the sake of the money. And Pharaoh hung his words upon what he saw, that Baal-zephon remained of all the gods of Egypt."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The phrase ״קָשָׁה יִרְאָתָם״ is obscure; translated hyper-literally as 'their fear is strong,' possibly referring to the Israelites' fear appearing as exploitable, or the idol's fearsome power. The context remains difficult."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:19:58.419009839Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}